Relative to the earliest recoverable DIALECT repository snapshot, later DIALECT
integration work preserves sample identifiers, repairs the expected tab-delimited
mutation input, accepts explicit input/output/auxiliary/interpreter paths,
parameterizes the PMF tail threshold, preserves high-count PMF values through
arbitrary-precision serialization, binds the cohort size to the authoritative
selected sample axis, and permits a PMF-only execution that stops before legacy
single-gene q-value reporting. The last functional cohort-axis boundary is DIALECT
commit d5883834a6ba52cf19145b5b26beecee9d2feaa2; the PMF-only execution change is
recorded by the revision-focused source commit and its run receipts.

